The `--ds` flag on a .ssl-named input whose content carries SSL markers:
classification is still by content, so it is an SSL-mode data source and
the data-source rules apply (no_default_statements_in_datasource on the
:DEFAULT line, plus datasource_default_required on the defaultless name).
Without `--ds` the same file is an ordinary script and the :DEFAULT layout
is correct.
-- input.ssl --
:PARAMETERS sCode;
:DEFAULT sCode, "NONE";
:RETURN Upper(sCode);
-- format [--ds] --
:PARAMETERS sCode;
:DEFAULT sCode, "NONE";
:RETURN Upper(sCode);
-- diagnostics [--ds] --
1:13-1:18 error datasource_default_required: Data source parameter 'sCode' needs an inline ':=' default; without one the data source fails when it runs (No default value for one or more parameters)
2:1-2:9 error no_default_statements_in_datasource: Data source files use inline ':=' defaults in ':PARAMETERS', not separate ':DEFAULT' statements
-- format --
:PARAMETERS sCode;
:DEFAULT sCode, "NONE";
:RETURN Upper(sCode);
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
